# Development Rules

1. Follow existing architecture.
2. Follow existing naming conventions.
3. Reuse existing services and components.
4. Never duplicate business logic.
5. Never create duplicate APIs.
6. Make minimal code changes.
7. Avoid changing unrelated files.
8. Keep code production ready.
9. Prefer existing patterns over creating new ones.
10. Generate clean, maintainable code.
11. Read only files directly related to the task.
12. Consider security implications.
13. Consider performance implications.

# Token Optimization

14. Do not analyze the entire project unless explicitly requested.
15. Do not explain architecture unless requested.
16. Do not generate reports unless requested.
17. Do not restate previous findings.
18. Do not explain obvious code changes.
19. Keep responses under 10 lines unless requested.
20. Investigate only the reported issue.
21. Read the minimum number of files required.
22. Do not create design documents automatically.
23. Do not summarize code unless requested.
24. Assume PROJECT_GUIDE.md is the source of truth.
25. Assume previous root-cause analysis is valid unless asked to re-check.

# Debug Mode

26. Reproduce the issue first.
27. Identify root cause.
28. If root cause is known, skip analysis.
29. Fix only the root cause.
30. Verify the fix.

# Output Format

31. Default output format:

Root cause:
...

Files changed:
...

Verification:
PASS/FAIL

32. No explanations unless requested.
33. No markdown reports unless requested.